WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.450
- This episode of Legal Eagle

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.120
was made possible by Skillshare.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.580
Learn to think like a lawyer
for free for two months

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.130
by clicking on the link
in the description.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.970
In the last few weeks,
we've seen defenders

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.630
of this administration go from

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.140
there was absolutely no quid pro quo.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.570
- There was no conditionality there,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.910
there was no quid pro quo there.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.990
- To it would only be a quid pro quo

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.220
if President Trump were
really thuggish about it.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.790
- Graham was asked what he thought

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.860
would constitute
inappropriate quid pro quo,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.767
saying "uh, hey pal, you know,

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.767
"you need to like, go after the Bidens

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.957
"or I ain't gonna give you any money.

00:00:32.957 --> 00:00:35.460
"He'd be really like thuggish about it."

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.390
- To quid pro quos happen
all the time and in fact,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.138
they're actually really good.

00:00:40.138 --> 00:00:42.010
- What you just described
is a quid pro quo,

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.810
it is funding will not flow
unless the investigation

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:50.290
into the democratic
server happened as well.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.770
- We do that all the
time with foreign policy.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.640
- So what's the deal with quid pro quos?

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.722
Impeachable offense or
routine diplomacy tool?

00:00:58.722 --> 00:01:01.472
(dramatic music)

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.560
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.220
You all took Latin in high school, right?

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.600
Everyone knows the legal
definition of quid pro quo

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.465
and we can just all go home, right?

00:01:11.465 --> 00:01:12.298
(buzzer buzzes)

00:01:12.298 --> 00:01:14.450
No, you want me to talk about
why this is all relevant?

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.110
Okay fine, on October 22nd, Bill Taylor,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.420
the top diplomat or charge
d'affaires to Ukraine

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.550
testified behind closed doors
before the House committees

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.620
that are leading the impeachment
inquiry of Donald Trump.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.510
Taylor's full testimony
is currently unknown,

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:32.550
but news agencies got ahold
of Taylor's opening statement.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.950
Now this was just Taylor's
opening statement,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.040
but what he revealed,

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.640
and it basically stunned
everyone that's paying attention.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.720
Taylor, you might recall,
was one of the diplomats

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.070
who was a party to a WhatsApp conversation

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.370
with US Special Envoy Kurt Volker

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.190
and US Ambassador to
the EU Gordon Sondland.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.670
Volker turned over the
transcripts of those texts

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.060
to the House committees.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.237
Taylor famously texted on September 9th,

00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:57.887
"As I said on the phone, I
think it's crazy to withhold

00:01:57.887 --> 00:02:00.660
"security assistance for help
with a political campaign,"

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.917
to when Gordon Sondland
replied five hours later,

00:02:03.917 --> 00:02:05.747
"Bill I believe you are incorrect about

00:02:05.747 --> 00:02:07.097
"President Trump's intentions.

00:02:07.097 --> 00:02:09.027
"The president has been crystal clear,

00:02:09.027 --> 00:02:10.977
"no quid pro quos of any kind.

00:02:10.977 --> 00:02:13.777
"The president whether
Ukraine is truly going to

00:02:13.777 --> 00:02:15.197
"adopt the transparency and reforms

00:02:15.197 --> 00:02:17.957
"that President Zelensky
promised during his campaign.

00:02:17.957 --> 00:02:20.457
"I suggest we stop the
back and forth by text.

00:02:20.457 --> 00:02:22.447
"If you still have concerns,
I recommend you give

00:02:22.447 --> 00:02:26.870
"Lisa Kenna or S a call to
discuss them directly, thanks."

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.040
Taylor was asked to testify as a witness

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.510
to the investigation into
the Trump administration's

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.180
efforts to pressure Ukrainian
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.810
into opening an investigation
into repudiated allegations

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.280
of Ukraine's interference in the 2016

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.060
US presidential elections,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.950
as well into the company Burisma

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.800
for the purpose of
eliciting or fabricating

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.900
dirt on Hunter Biden,
and by proxy, Joe Biden,

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.340
political candidate president
of the United States.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.790
Taylor began his opening
statement by emphasizing

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.800
the importance of the
United States's relationship

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.327
with Ukraine, saying "our
national security demands

00:02:59.327 --> 00:03:01.490
"that this relationship remain strong."

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.920
Taylor went on to say more about this,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.070
noting that Ukraine now
and for the last five years

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.930
has been under attack from Russia,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.590
and that the United
States security assistance

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.300
is crucial to Ukraine's
defense against Russia,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.190
and that withholding security assistance

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.710
would be, quote, crazy.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.200
And crazy is exactly what
Taylor would soon discover

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.630
on the part of the Trump administration.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.250
In June, Taylor delivered a
letter from President Trump

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.150
to President Zelensky congratulating him

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.350
on his election victory and inviting him

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.430
to a meeting at the Oval Office.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.480
This meeting was an
apparent goal for Zelensky,

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.030
but in order to obtain this goal,

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.820
Zelensky had to do some
things for Trump first.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.160
For example, in a planned June 28th call

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.200
with Ukrainian president,
Ambassador Sondland,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.817
quote, "did not wish
to include most of the

00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:46.440
"regular inter agency participants,"

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.427
and, quote, "said that
he wanted to make sure

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.237
"no one was transcribing or monitoring

00:03:50.237 --> 00:03:52.730
"as they added President
Zelensky to the call."

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.270
Taylor noted that a short time later,

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.367
it became abundantly
clear to him that, quote,

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.147
"the meeting President
Zelensky wanted was conditioned

00:03:59.147 --> 00:04:01.637
"on the investigations of
Burisma and the alleged

00:04:01.637 --> 00:04:04.970
"Ukrainian interference
in the 2016 US elections,"

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.490
and that this, quote,
irregular policy channel

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.860
was guided by Rudy Giuliani.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.520
On July 18th, Taylor
learned from an individual

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.967
at the Office of Management
and Budget, the OMB,

00:04:14.967 --> 00:04:18.330
that there was a hold on
security assistance to Ukraine.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.130
This individual could not explain why

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.710
there was a hold, but Taylor
had a pretty good idea.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.670
When Taylor inquired further,
the individual told him that

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:28.187
her boss had, quote,
"instructed her not to approve

00:04:28.187 --> 00:04:30.527
"any additional spending
of security assistance

00:04:30.527 --> 00:04:32.870
"for Ukraine until further notice."

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.250
This unidentified individual also relayed

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.020
that the directive for the hold had come

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.760
directly from President
Trump through Mick Mulvaney

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.120
to the OMB's chief of staff.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.380
This is very, very bad, and
we'll talk about in a moment

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.090
this is strong evidence
for a quid pro quo.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.060
In his statement, Taylor
went on to emphasize

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.460
how important US aid to Ukraine was

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.610
and how many more lives could
be lost if the hold remained.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.780
He also noted that the
Secretary of Defense,

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.810
Secretary of State, the CIA Director,

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.820
and the National Security
Advisor all tried to sit down

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.830
with President Trump and
convince him to release the hold.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.847
This sit-down, however, was quote,

00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:09.260
"hard to schedule."
(buzzer buzzes)

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.440
What President Trump
wanted, Taylor discovered,

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.587
was for Zelensky to, quote,
"say that he will help

00:05:14.587 --> 00:05:16.747
"the investigation and
address any specific

00:05:16.747 --> 00:05:19.280
"personnel issues if there are any."

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.540
Trump's administration wanted
Zelensky to publicly announce

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.720
his participation in this investigation,

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.980
and they even tried to
give Zelensky a script

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.600
of what to say to Trump,
suggesting that he announce

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.110
that, quote, "I will
leave no stone unturned"

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.680
with regard to, quote "investigations,"

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.850
all the while making it look
like the US was uninvolved.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.800
Zelensky's response, according
to Taylor, to all of this

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.787
was that he did not want to, quote,

00:05:42.787 --> 00:05:46.730
"be used as a pawn in a
US reelection scheme."

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.150
This testimony paints a picture

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.050
of the Trump administration's motivations.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.770
By withholding US aid,
they hope to get Zelensky

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.840
to announce his investigation
into Joe Biden's son

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.240
in the hopes that it would bolster

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.940
Trump's reelection campaign.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.190
At this point, the clock was ticking

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.510
with regard to security
assistance to Ukraine.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.470
Because of the way the US budget works,

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.720
if the funds weren't released
by the end of September,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.130
they would essentially
expire and disappear,

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.080
not to mention the actual Ukrainians

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.380
whose lives were at stake.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.530
In the last five years, 13,000
Ukrainians have been killed

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.160
by Russian soldiers,
and potentially dozens

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.400
of Ukrainian civilians
had been killed by Russia

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.980
during this time period.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.727
Taylor was worried
especially because, quote,

00:06:23.727 --> 00:06:25.697
"if the White House did not lift the hold

00:06:25.697 --> 00:06:28.157
"prior to the end of the
fiscal year, September 30th,

00:06:28.157 --> 00:06:31.080
"the funds would expire and
Ukraine would receive nothing."

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.010
As the wait went on, Ambassador
Sondland explicitly stated

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:36.217
that, quote, "the
security assistance money

00:06:36.217 --> 00:06:38.877
"would not come until
President Zelensky committed

00:06:38.877 --> 00:06:41.480
"to pursue the Burisma investigation."

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.890
Taylor's fears were confirmed.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.360
This was the first time that he had heard

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.200
that security assistance,
not just a White House

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.860
Oval Office meeting was conditioned

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:52.000
on Zelensky committing
to investigating Burisma.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.820
The bottom line is that Taylor testified

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:56.370
that one, there was in
fact a quid pro quo.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:57.960
The White House conditioned the release

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.580
of $400 million of military
aid on Ukraine's statement

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.200
that they were opening
investigation into Burisma.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.170
Number two, the order to withhold aid

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.190
came from the president himself.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:11.110
Number three, this was
never about corruption,

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.280
it was about getting dirt
on Joe Biden and his son,

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.060
and number four, the
White House tried to hide

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.630
their involvement by scripting
Ukraine's announcement

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.440
and pretending that the investigations

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.250
had been Ukraine's idea all along.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.090
It's of course always
important to take a step back

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.510
and look at the various players.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.980
Everyone has bias, and
it's important to recognize

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.400
when you have two conflicting accounts.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.210
Taylor is a career
diplomat who served in both

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.890
republican and democratic administrations,

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.590
so could he be too close to Ukraine?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:42.130
Of course, interestingly,
Secretary of State Mike Pompeo

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.890
specifically asked Taylor to essentially

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:46.920
come out of retirement to
help with the situation.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.830
Taylor was essentially
President Trump's pick

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.030
to run diplomacy with the Ukraine.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.000
Taylor acknowledged his
own bias and stated that

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.970
he wanted the US to support
Ukraine, and conditioned

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.500
his coming out of retirement
on that very fact.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.510
On the other side of the coin,

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.840
there is Gordon Sondland who is a hotelier

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.650
who donated a million dollars
to Trump's inauguration.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.370
Allegedly when Gordon Sondland testified

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:09.330
behind closed doors,
he did not recall most

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.100
of what Bill Taylor testified to,

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.150
although he doesn't appear
to outright contradict

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:15.280
anything that Bill Taylor actually said.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.420
Taylor allegedly took
contemporaneous notes

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.690
throughout the affair.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.830
In addition to Bill Taylor's testimony,

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.840
Lieutenant Colonel Alexander Vindman,

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.680
an army officer assigned to
the National Security Council,

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.400
also testified recently.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.220
He was one of the members of the NSC

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:32.160
that listened to the
infamous July 25th call

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.530
from the situation room.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.270
According to his opening statement,

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:37.970
Vindman largely confirmed the
account of the whistleblower

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.290
and the readout that has
already been made public,

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.540
and which I covered in an earlier video.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.560
Vindman testified in his opening statement

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.120
that he was, quote,
"concerned by the call,"

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.337
stating "I did not think
it was proper to demand

00:08:49.337 --> 00:08:51.877
"that a foreign government
investigate a US citizen,

00:08:51.877 --> 00:08:53.647
"and I was worried about the implications

00:08:53.647 --> 00:08:55.847
"for the US government's
support of Ukraine.

00:08:55.847 --> 00:08:58.087
"I realized that if Ukraine
pursued an investigation

00:08:58.087 --> 00:09:00.467
"into the Bidens and
Burisma, it would likely be

00:09:00.467 --> 00:09:02.857
"interpreted as a partisan
play which would undoubtedly

00:09:02.857 --> 00:09:05.507
"result in Ukraine losing
the bipartisan support

00:09:05.507 --> 00:09:07.477
"it had thus fair maintained.

00:09:07.477 --> 00:09:10.047
"This would all undermine
US national security.

00:09:10.047 --> 00:09:11.787
"Following the call, I again reported

00:09:11.787 --> 00:09:14.380
"my concerns to NSC's lead counsel."

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.220
The New York Times is also reporting that

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.700
Vindman stated in his deposition,

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.490
which lasted 10 and a half hours,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.330
and that's quite a long time,

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.410
that he requested several
changes to the wording

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.830
of the read-out of the call,

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.470
but that those changes were rejected

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.570
by the White House for unknown reasons.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:31.700
Vindman also testified about
an earlier July 10th call

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.830
with Oleksandr Danylyuk, the
Secretary of the National

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.880
Security and Defense Council for Ukraine,

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.020
and National Security Advisor Bolton,

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.750
Ambassadors Volker and Sondland

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.680
and Energy Secretary Rick Perry.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.990
Vindman testified that
during this July 10th call,

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:48.130
the meeting proceeded well
until the Ukrainians broached

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.510
the subject of a meeting
between the two presidents.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.570
Ambassador Sondland started to speak about

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.660
delivering specific
investigations in order to

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.520
secure the meeting with the president,

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:59.550
at which time, Ambassador
Bolton cut the meeting short.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.950
Following this meeting, there
was a scheduled debriefing

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.290
during which Ambassador
Sondland emphasized

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:07.160
the importance that Ukraine
deliver the investigations

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.811
into the 2016 election,
the Bidens, and Burisma.

00:10:10.811 --> 00:10:13.750
I stated to Ambassador
Sondland that his statements

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.840
were inappropriate, that the
request to investigate Biden

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:19.750
and his son had nothing to
do with national security,

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.840
and that such investigations
were not something

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.840
the NSC was going to
get involved in or push.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.040
Dr. Hill then entered
the room and asserted

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.340
to Ambassador Sondland that

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.080
his statements were inappropriate.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.620
Following the debriefing
meeting, I reported my concerns

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.480
to the NSC's lead counsel.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.430
Dr. Hill also reported the incident

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:37.890
to the NSC's lead counsel.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:40.700
So in general, Lieutenant
Colonel Vindman's testimony

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.660
backs up Bill Taylor's
and refutes the testimony

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.500
of Ambassador Gordon Sondland.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.720
Additionally, there have
been attacks from the right

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.690
against Lieutenant Colonel Vindman

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:52.050
for his status as a Ukrainian immigrant

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:54.986
and allegations of dual loyalty,

00:10:54.986 --> 00:10:57.100
despite the fact that he's a US citizen

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.870
and long-time member of the Army.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.950
It's the clear that these
attacks or criticisms

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.180
are based on anything
more than speculation.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.220
So that brings us to the quid pro quo.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.080
Now of course, in the
famous Sondland text,

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.730
Sondland relayed that the
president has been crystal clear

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.200
that no quid pro quos of any kind,

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.300
but just because they claim
that doesn't necessarily

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.910
mean that it not a quid
pro quo arrangement.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.031
As Taylor himself said in
response to this contention,

00:11:23.031 --> 00:11:25.957
quote "President Trump did
insist that President Zelensky

00:11:25.957 --> 00:11:28.787
"go to a microphone and say
he is opening investigations

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:31.437
"of Burisma and 2016
election interference,

00:11:31.437 --> 00:11:35.200
"and that President Zelensky
would want to do this himself."

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.930
Quid pro quo translates
literally to this for that.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.240
It is a type of exchange
where someone on one side

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.130
gives a thing of value to someone else

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.630
and expects something in
return from that person.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.330
Whether a quid pro quo
is illegal and illicit

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.930
depends on the context.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.470
If I give you five dollars
and you give me a book,

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:54.240
that's a quid pro quo, and
there's nothing wrong with that,

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.370
but things take a turn
when you're talking about

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.690
government officials using
power of their office

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.950
to extract a personal benefit.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.670
Oftentimes, a quid pro quo
emerges in a governmental

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.280
setting when a government
official receives something

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:09.330
of personal value and
then abuses his or her

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.670
official power to give something in return

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.370
to that specific constituent who gave

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.990
some personal benefit to
that government official.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.810
You can imagine a government
contractor who gives

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.590
a fancy new sports car
to a government official

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:24.210
who then steers a valuable
governmental contract

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:28.153
to that contractor, that
is a classic quid pro quo.

00:12:28.153 --> 00:12:31.130
Illegal quid pro quo
arrangements also tend to pop up

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.430
in the workplace setting.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.840
A quid pro quo would
exist where an employer

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:37.060
demands sexual favors in return for

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.850
an employee keeping their job.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.700
So it depends on the context.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.920
Mick Mulvaney has
recently been emphasizing

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.380
that especially in
foreign policy settings,

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.530
quid pro quo arrangements
happen all the time,

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.630
that's just the nature of foreign policy.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.100
- We do that all the
time with foreign policy.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.510
- I'll help you do this
if you help me do that.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:55.900
Everyone is happy and secure.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.810
For example, throughout the
history of the United States,

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.950
we have used our own aid
or assistance as leverage

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.770
for achieving things
such as democracy abroad,

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:05.930
an end to corruption,
and even physical access

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.990
to important geographical areas.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.640
For example, President Jimmy
Carter provided Egypt with aid

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.110
in exchange for Egypt
making peace with Israel.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.810
President Bush even demanded
that countries provide

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.560
free speech and freedom of assembly

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.020
before receiving certain US aid.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.770
However, while this may be true,

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:25.050
quid pro quos that involve
a concerted self-interest

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.700
for a particular politician
do not happen all the time

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.530
in foreign policy, and quite frankly,

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.620
they really don't happen at all.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.720
In fact, it was such a stunning admission

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.040
by mick Mulvaney to admit
that this was a quid pro quo

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.830
on behalf of the Trump administration,

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.160
ostensibly for President Trump,

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:44.420
that it elicited an
almost immediate walk-back

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.640
from Mulvaney and the rest
of the administration.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.760
This arrangement between
the Trump administration

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.290
and President Zelensky of Ukraine
falls into the problematic

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:55.560
category of quid pro quos
for a couple of reasons.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.630
First of all, such an
arrangement is probably

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.770
highly illegal and may be sufficient

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.580
to prove the crimes of bribery
and election interference.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.760
While it was would admittedly
difficult to indict

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.040
and convict a president of these crimes

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.750
for reasons that we've already
talked about on this channel,

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.020
in order to establish a
prima facie case for bribery

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:15.280
under 18 USC 201, one
would have to prove that

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:17.490
a public official, in
this case President Trump,

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.800
directly or indirectly corruptly demanded

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.780
anything of value personally,

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.220
in this case bolstering
his reelection campaign,

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.310
in return for being
influenced in the performance

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:29.310
of any official act, in this case,

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.870
releasing money that
Congress and the Pentagon

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.270
had already appropriated for Ukraine.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:38.660
Or you can take, for
example, 51 USC 30121,

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.247
which states that "it shall
be unlawful for a foreign

00:14:41.247 --> 00:14:44.227
"national, directly or
indirectly, to make a contribution

00:14:44.227 --> 00:14:47.017
"or donation of money
or other thing of value

00:14:47.017 --> 00:14:49.347
"or to make an express or implied promise

00:14:49.347 --> 00:14:51.847
"to make a contribution
or donation in connection

00:14:51.847 --> 00:14:54.390
"with a federal, state,
or local election."

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.760
In this case, one would
argue that the thing of value

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.270
is investigating a political rival,

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.370
which obviously the Trump administration

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:05.050
would try to lord over
the head of Joe Biden

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.360
as he tries to secure
the democratic nomination

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.385
for potentially running for

00:15:10.385 --> 00:15:12.520
President of the United States in 2020.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:15.180
Additionally and apart from
whether any of these acts

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.306
fit the neat statutory
definitions of these crimes,

00:15:18.306 --> 00:15:20.490
and overcome the constitutional issues

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.900
in terms of indicting a sitting president,

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.110
this arrangement is problematic because

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.380
it essentially means that the
President of the United States

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.930
is subverting the national interest

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.250
for his own personal interest.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.190
In other words, he's putting himself

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:36.450
above the entire country.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.090
Now, no one argues that
Hunter Biden's status

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:42.350
as a board member of Burisma
doesn't smack of nepotism,

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:45.580
but strong-arming a sovereign
nation into investigating

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.470
a conspiracy theory about
Ukrainian computer servers

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:52.040
and ginning up a defunct
investigation into Burisma

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.490
appears to serve President Trump only,

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.660
and not US national interest.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:59.110
It appears motivated
primarily if not solely

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:00.830
to help President Trump get reelected

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.540
and not to help America.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.440
Rudy Giuliani tweets
the quiet part out loud

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.137
when he tweeted "with all the fake news,

00:16:07.137 --> 00:16:09.267
"let me make it clear
that everything I did

00:16:09.267 --> 00:16:11.637
"was to discover evidence
to defend my client

00:16:11.637 --> 00:16:13.227
"against false charges.

00:16:13.227 --> 00:16:15.297
"Dems would be horrified
by the attacks on me,

00:16:15.297 --> 00:16:17.297
"if my client was a terrorist,
but they don't believe

00:16:17.297 --> 00:16:19.780
"real Donald Trump has rights."

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.490
The problem here is that at
the request of the president,

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.040
Rudy Giuliani was running his own shadow

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.270
foreign policy operation,
and he's admitting that

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:32.034
in this context, he wasn't
acting on behalf of America,

00:16:32.034 --> 00:16:35.570
but acting on behalf of
his client, Donald Trump,

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.270
in trying to get dirt
against a political rival.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:41.210
If this had been in America's
interest, President Trump

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:43.790
would have used the usual
diplomatic channels,

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.960
gone through the Mutual
Legal Assistance Treaty

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:48.350
and avoided using an entirely separate

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:52.190
clandestine shadow foreign
policy team led by Rudy Giuliani.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.420
This kind of arrangement
pressuring Ukraine

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:57.650
to do something to benefit
President Trump personally

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:01.717
in exchange for $400 million
in US aid and assistance

00:17:01.717 --> 00:17:05.060
is what appears to be an abuse of power

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:08.291
and an attempt to use one's
official capacity as president

00:17:08.291 --> 00:17:09.960
(bell dings)
for personal gain.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.400
Now some, including former
acting Attorney General

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.500
Matthew Whitaker have argued that

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.970
an abuse of power is not a crime.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.560
- What evidence of a crime do you have?

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.690
I mean, the constitution,
you know, sort of,

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:23.520
abuse of power is not a crime.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.810
The constitution is very
clear that this has to be

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.830
some pretty egregious behavior.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:31.210
- However, such an abuse of
power is a crucial inquiry

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:33.130
as far as impeachment is concerned.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:34.940
That's because impeachment was designed

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:37.340
to dismantle this kind of abuse of power.

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.890
Ironically, Bill Taylor
came out of retirement

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.823
at the request of Mike
Pompeo to help Ukraine.

00:17:42.823 --> 00:17:46.040
Now he'll probably want to
go back into retirement,

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.780
and now that he has
more time on his hands,

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.620
maybe he'll finally
listen to his grandkids

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.550
and join Instagram after
taking Brandon Woelfel's class

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.510
Instagram-Worthy Photography,
Shoot, Edit, and Share.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.940
Or maybe he will finally
tackle all those chores

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.720
around the house his wife asked him to do,

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.280
like redesigning his family room.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.720
He could really use Emily Henderson's

